    "lineStart": 0,
    "memoText": "\n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 249\n\nTO THE SENATE:\n\nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n\nSenate Bill Number 1555, entitled:\n\n    \"AN ACT establishing a moratorium on the department of environmental\n      conservation's  plan  to declare mute swans a \"prohibited invasive\n      species\"; and providing for the repeal  of  such  provisions  upon\n      expiration thereof\"\n\n    NOT APPROVED\n\n  This bill would require that, before adopting any mute swan management\nplan,  the  Department of Environmental Conservation (DEC) hold at least\ntwo public hearings in areas with mute swan populations, and  include  a\npublic  comment  period  of  at  least 45 days following the last public\nhearing. The bill would also require that  any  management  plan,  at  a\nminimum, give priority for non-lethal management techniques.\n\n  I  vetoed  similar legislation last year because it was duplicative of\nefforts that DEC has already undertaken regarding its mute swan  manage-\nment  plan.  The circumstances that necessitated my disapproval have not\nchanged. DEC has already announced that it  would  revise  its  proposed\nplan to acknowledge regional differences, potential impacts, and desired\npopulation  goals  for  each region of New York, as well as to emphasize\nthe use of non-lethal methods to reduce the  population.  DEC  also  met\nwith  dozens  of stakeholder groups to discuss revisions to the plan. In\nMarch 2015, DEC published a revised  draft  plan  for  a  45-day  public\ncomment  period,  which addressed the concerns raised by the public. DEC\nhas received over 8,000 public comments on the  plan  and  is  currently\nundertaking  a  rigorous  review  of  those comments. For these reasons,\nadditional public hearings and another comment  period  are  unnecessary\nand I am therefore vetoing this bill.\n\n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n\n                               __________\n",
